+Add {func}`scanpy.pp.normalize_shifted_clr` for PFlog shifted centered log-ratio normalization, a variance-stabilizing, depth-invariant and rank-preserving count transform {cite:p}`Booeshaghi2022`. By default, it estimates negative-binomial overdispersion and uses the Anscombe pseudocount. The complete centered result is stored in `X` or the selected layer. Because CLR centering generally maps zeros to non-zero values, the output is dense. {smaller}`R Baber`
